From 2360171699c3910ea9e3dc80ede10dc31efbcb6f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 00:40:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): keep recovery park identity causal across
 reconcile restores [daveey]

Reconcile re-inserts a lost task_events row under a newer local id while keeping
its uid. Recovery authority read MAX(id)/created-id order, so a restored park
made its own valid recovery requester look stale, a restored stale requester's
created event looked fresh, and a restored older park displaced the current one.

On boards with a uid column, lifecycle, receipt and created events now carry
append-time evidence (_recovery_history_v1): a stable identity, the lifecycle
heads they superseded, the receipts a park cites, and the creator-chain parks a
new card observed. Readers take the unique evidenced head instead of insertion
order; freshness is 'created while this park was current'. Legacy synced
histories with no evidence fail closed for authority but keep their triage
hold. Unsynced boards keep local-id order unchanged.
---
